+# Add t and validate PlaceBlock arguments with it
+
+Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker as a package and switches the
+`PlaceBlock` remote handler from hand-written argument checks to a t check. Remotes added later
+can use the same package.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `pesde.toml`: adds `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }`, installed from Wally
+  through pesde like the other packages. 3.1.1 is the latest version on the Wally index and has no
+  dependencies. It installs into `roblox_packages`, so it shows up as
+  `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau`: `onPlaceBlock` checks its arguments with
+  `t.tuple(t.string, isVector3WithoutNaN)`. `t.Vector3` only checks `typeof`, so
+  `isVector3WithoutNaN` wraps it and still rejects a position with a NaN component.
+- `README.md`: adds t to the package table.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+Every check the handler made before still runs, in the same order, and each still drops the
+request without an error:
+
+| Check | Before | Now |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof(...) ~= "string"` | `t.string` in the tuple |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof(...) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` inside `isVector3WithoutNaN` |
+| Position has no NaN component | `position ~= position` | `value ~= value` inside `isVector3WithoutNaN` |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | unchanged |
+| Rate limit (`MIN_INTERVAL`) | | unchanged |
+| Character has a `HumanoidRootPart` | | unchanged |
+| Cell is not below Y = 0 and not occupied | | unchanged |
+| Cell within `MAX_REACH` | | unchanged |
+
+t checks don't narrow Luau types, so the handler casts `blockTypeName :: string` and
+`position :: Vector3` after the check passes.
+
+## Before testing
+
+`pesde.lock` is **not** updated in this PR. The package wasn't installed when the change was
+written, so do this first:
+
+1. Stop `rojo serve` (an install rewrites `roblox_packages`, and Rojo 7.7.x can crash on that).
+2. From the repo root, run `pesde install`. This installs t and updates `pesde.lock`.
+3. Commit the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch.
+4. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp can type t:
+   `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`
+5. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo plugin. Confirm `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`
+   exists in the place.
+
+Without step 2, `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)` fails and `BlockPlacement` errors when it
+loads, so blocks can't be placed at all.
+
+## How to test
+
+Run the checks from the README (`luau-lsp analyze`, `selene src`, `stylua --check src`) after the
+install. Before the install, `stylua` and `selene` passed on the changed script. `luau-lsp`
+reported one error, `Unknown require: game/ReplicatedStorage/Packages/t`, because t wasn't
+installed yet; it should clear after the steps above.
+
+Then in a playtest:
+
+- Placing blocks from the client still works.
+- With the command bar switched to the client during a playtest, fire
+  `ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock` with bad arguments. Each of these should place nothing and log
+  no error:
+  - `FireServer(123, Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (name isn't a string)
+  - `FireServer("Brick", "0,4,0")` (position isn't a Vector3)
+  - `FireServer("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))` (NaN component)
+  - `FireServer("Lava", Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (unknown block type)
+- `FireServer("Brick", <a cell next to your character>)` places a Brick block.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
